Let F: X ⊆ R'' -> R'' be any force field. 
Then x₀ ∈ X is called an equilibrium point of F if F(x₀) = 0. 
An equilibrium point x₀ is said to be stable if, for every r, e > 0, we can find other numbers r₀, e₀ > 0 such that if we place a paritcle at position x with ||x - x₀|| < r₀ and provide it with a kinetic energy less than e₀, then the particle will always remain within distance r of x₀ with kinetic energy less than e. 
